// Material 3 Expressive design tokens.
//
// Colors are generated by matugen (SchemeContent) from the wallpaper into
// style/Colors.json. FileView watches that file, so `matugen image ...`
// recolors the bar live, without a reload. If the file is absent, the
// Material baseline dark scheme below is used as-is.
//
// Light and dark are two matugen files: Colors.json (dark, written by the
// wallpaper pass in ~/.config/matugen/config.toml) and ColorsLight.json (light,
// written by the second `matugen -m light` run below — matugen takes the mode
// from the command line only, a per-template `mode` is ignored). Both files are
// watched, so a wallpaper change recolors the bar in either mode; switching
// ShellState.themeMode just swaps which file feeds the tokens.
//
// Two style packs share these tokens (ShellState.styleMode, switched in the
// settings menu): "m3" is the wallpaper palette above; "new" swaps in fixed
// graphite surfaces with acrylic alpha, flat text tones, a hairline edge with
// an inner rim and a neutral drop shadow, while the accents stay
// wallpaper-derived. Every style-dependent token hangs off `glass`, so the M3
// look is untouched.
//
// ShellState.colorScheme picks the palette source: "matugen" (the file above),
// "oled" (strict black/white) or "gruvbox" (Gruvbox). Each fixed pack has a
// light twin, picked by ShellState.themeMode along with the light baseline;
// they replace the "new" surfaces as well, so a picked scheme always shows.
